From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:05:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/apple-dart: adopt J713 display streams with retained
 ownership

Adopt retained J713 display streams without resetting their live firmware
roots. Validate inherited leaf ownership against consumer reservations and
Linux memory, keep DMA provenance through quarantine, and retain uncertain
backing until reboot. Attach the shared fault interrupt only after both
display DARTs are admitted; partial admission leaves it unobserved.

Unify strict-DMA and fault-quarantine predicates with retained radio SIDs
without sharing their hardware ownership. Refuse masked display faults,
quarantine both display peers before releasing their shared IRQ, and adapt
the scoped radio regression harness. Keep display reset explicitly blocked.

Generated-by: Codex
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
[dylan: apple_dart_t8110_hw_invalidate_tlb(): kept omacom's fw_handoff slot
 guard after the borrowed-display check, as on integration/aurora. The
 bcm4377-radio-sids.py selftest update is dropped with the selftest itself
 (Bluetooth part of 0877cd766 not taken).]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
